{
  "_comment": [
    "Validate-mode golden: design §5.2's Mandates/Constraints drift",
    "check, over hand-written IR (no Clang needed, so this runs on every",
    "lane).",
    "",
    "`gadget`'s copy constructor carries an authored `\\mandates` and a",
    "derived Mandates conjunct asserting the same thing -- the duplicate",
    "case. `widget`'s constructor template carries a derived Constraints",
    "conjunct (`copyable<T>` is `true`) contradicted by authored prose",
    "reading `false` -- the contradict case.",
    "",
    "Three negative controls, which must stay silent alongside those two:",
    "`gadget`'s destructor is a derived Mandates element with no authored",
    "twin at all; `widget`'s second constructor is an authored Constraints",
    "element that names a different subject than its derived twin; and",
    "`gadget`'s own roster carries one genuinely undocumented member",
    "(`scratch`), included so this fixture has an Error-severity finding --",
    "run-golden.cmake's MODE validate requires exit code 1, and the drift",
    "check alone never produces one (design §5.2: \"validator warns\").",
    "",
    "The `conjuncts` field on each authored replacement is the suppressed",
    "derivation's pre-join list (frontend.cpp); it is",
    "what lets the check point at the specific assert rather than a joined",
    "sentence with no conjunct boundaries left in it."
  ],
